This policy explains what <%= shop %> collects when you visit or buy from our shop, and what we do with it.

## What we collect

- What you give us at checkout: your name, email, shipping address, phone number (optional) and order details.
- Payment details are entered on our payment provider's page (Stripe). We never see or store your card number.
- Basic technical information, such as your browser and the pages you visit, to keep the shop working and secure.

## How we use it

To make and ship your order, to email you about it (confirmation, shipping and tracking), to answer your questions, and to prevent fraud. We don't sell your personal information.

## Who we share it with

Only the companies that help us run the shop: our payment provider, the print partner that makes your item, and the carriers that deliver it, each only with what they need.

## How long we keep it

We keep order records as long as the law requires for accounting and taxes, then delete them.

## Your rights

You can ask us for a copy of your data, to correct it, or to delete it, by emailing <%= contact %>. Depending on where you live (for example the EU, UK or California) you may have further rights, which we respect.

## Changes

We may update this policy; the latest version is always on this page.
